Stop the build when a build-time tool fails.

Two kinds of rule went on after their tool failed:
- programs/localized/templates/*.am: "TOOL ... > $@ || $(RM) $@" removes
  the half-made target and succeeds, so make goes on without the
  app-defaults file, catalogue or action file, which is then missing from
  the install. Now "|| { $(RM) $@; exit 1; }".
- programs/tttypes/Makefile.am: "tt_type_comp ... && touch $@ ; $(RM)
  .tt_lock" takes its status from the rm, so a failed type compile left
  types.xdr short without a word. Now the rule removes .tt_lock and fails
  when tt_type_comp fails, and touches the stamp only after it succeeds.
A successful build makes the same files as before.

